      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): reject malformed history offsets",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users requesting `sessions_history` pagination could pass malformed string offsets such as `\"1abc\"` and have them accepted as offset `1` instead of being rejected before `chat.history` dispatch.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth the public `sessions_history` tool and the embedded `chat.history` gateway stub now reuse the existing strict non-negative integer parameter reader for `offset`, matching the schema contract and the strict `limit` parsing already used in the same paths. This keeps the fix local to the session history owner boundary and avoids changing pagination behavior for valid numeric offsets.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMalformed offset values are rejected consistently, so session-history pagination cannot silently run from a different page than the caller requested.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: malformed string offsets are rejected in both the public `sessions_history` tool path and the embedded `chat.history` gateway stub path, before malformed pagination can dispatch or read history.\n- Current-head real behavior proof at `ea64b57a1a00168496b178f2a97b8932dc22f33a`: `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` invoked `createSessionsHistoryTool().execute(...)` and `createEmbeddedCallGateway()({ method: \"chat.history\", ... })` with `offset: \"1abc\"`.\n\n```text\nHEAD ea64b57a1a00168496b178f2a97b8932dc22f33a\nsessions_history offset=\"1abc\": rejected name=ToolInputError message=\"offset must be a non-negative integer\"\nsessions_history gateway dispatched=false\nembedded chat.history offset=\"1abc\": rejected name=ToolInputError message=\"offset must be a non-negative integer\"\n```\n\n- Focused regression tests: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/sessions-history-tool.test.ts src/agents/tools/embedded-gateway-stub.test.ts` passed with 2 files and 27 tests.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Branch refresh: `git rev-list --count HEAD..upstream/main` returned `0` at proof time after merging current `upstream/main`.",
